{"id": "EUVD-2026-86914", "enisaUuid": "899285c3-b502-3807-974a-04ddf5aa60a2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: backtracking shouldn't clear outer frame R1-R5 for callbacks\n\nWhen processing calls to bpf_loop() verifier marks R1 (and R4) as\nprecise. R1 tracks loop iterations number and because of the\n'callback_depth < R1' mechanics in check_helper_call() must be marked\nprecise. However, precision propagation for R1 was broken,\nwhen bpf_loop() call was verified on a second iteration.\n\nConsider the following verification trace:\n- main: bpf_loop(nr_loops, callback ...)\n- callback: BPF_EXIT\n- main: bpf_loop(nr_loops, callback ...)\n- ...\n\nWhile the first visit of the call to bpf_loop() propagated R1\nprecision as expected, the second call to mark_chain_precision() in\nthe check_helper_call() set R1, but it was immediately reset when\nbacktrack_insn() processed preceding BPF_EXIT in the loop deleted in\nthis patch.\n\nBecause of that, the second visit of the call to bpf_loop() injected\ncheckpoint with R1 not marked as precise. Which could trick the\nverifier into accepting unsafe programs. See the next patch for an\nexample of such program.\n\nCommit is structured in a way to minimize conflicts when\n'bpf' would be eventually merged with 'bpf-next'.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:24:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:25", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ac58dab0a83d2c64e3b807a3a0b399f17a74110", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cdc93c6370f792d0649df2a145ac0cdcd430e411", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3a39bc9707fbd1bef4df7318a9d02222741dda5b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f83890dfed9efc5e19df1dbc1ad707a142936923", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e3e4f66cc4b72333d0886ae2673c360248987889"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98084", "GHSA-hcwg-2fch-4v4c"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03646d31-6189-3869-9836-cdd6eecf8eaf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "07a31c18-9d93-3340-8b90-fd3c31992c89", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "0e7a871a-38bf-37c5-a81d-04b31f8ffe3a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.7"}, {"id": "0fb0d307-7d27-3b1b-94a5-b72a5842581d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ab5cfac139ab8576fb54630d4cca23c3e690ee90 <cdc93c6370f792d0649df2a145ac0cdcd430e411"}, {"id": "13ecb60c-8b7a-371c-a291-bded8e00fea6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "1efa689b-b56b-3c87-aac9-f3c59f4df0f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ab5cfac139ab8576fb54630d4cca23c3e690ee90 <e3e4f66cc4b72333d0886ae2673c360248987889"}, {"id": "43ef04bd-710d-3f1d-b5af-e414e5561148", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "99fee045-d0c2-3427-ac26-bbfc311e4516", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "c5ca0edf-37cc-360e-a49c-bf3000630660", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ab5cfac139ab8576fb54630d4cca23c3e690ee90 <f83890dfed9efc5e19df1dbc1ad707a142936923"}, {"id": "d373323e-1ae2-3038-931f-98ea683179dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.15 <6.6.160"}, {"id": "e7c069e9-a2ed-351c-8cea-9b94f5442506", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ab5cfac139ab8576fb54630d4cca23c3e690ee90 <3a39bc9707fbd1bef4df7318a9d02222741dda5b"}, {"id": "f33f93c7-fc58-3131-9afc-3e66fecb9ec9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b43550d7d58e7ae6618aaab18c1e912fa4d6e3dd <1ac58dab0a83d2c64e3b807a3a0b399f17a74110"}, {"id": "f508ac0c-22de-33f2-8570-316bf6e82849", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9124c75e-15fe-3657-a3b1-810c4f52a5ab", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}